WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.463 --> 00:00:14.471
- [Narrator] The $500,000 Family.

00:00:14.471 --> 00:00:16.231
It's not about skill level.

00:00:16.231 --> 00:00:17.840
For the most part, it's about an

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.527
eagerness to help others,

00:00:19.527 --> 00:00:23.837
to be loving and make others
feel comfortable; like family.

00:00:23.837 --> 00:00:27.590
Sharon Galor, founder
of Toronto Dance Salsa.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.413
When Sharon first walked into a salsa club

00:00:29.413 --> 00:00:30.587
and took to the floor,

00:00:30.587 --> 00:00:32.327
she was terrible.

00:00:32.327 --> 00:00:34.565
She was so bad that one of of the guys

00:00:34.565 --> 00:00:35.983
who asked her to dance,

00:00:35.983 --> 00:00:37.152
left her in the middle of a song.

00:00:37.152 --> 00:00:39.807
Now while that hurt, it didn't matter.

00:00:39.807 --> 00:00:41.680
Despite her limited dancing ability,

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.068
she felt at home there

00:00:43.068 --> 00:00:45.590
because she loved the people.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:46.918
After only a week of dancing,

00:00:46.918 --> 00:00:48.343
she had a group of new friends

00:00:48.343 --> 00:00:51.008
and instantly felt like she belonged.

00:00:51.008 --> 00:00:54.886
She had fallen in love with
salsa and it's community.

00:00:54.886 --> 00:00:56.702
Meanwhile, she was on
the fast track to success

00:00:56.702 --> 00:00:58.783
in her corporate HR career.

00:00:58.783 --> 00:01:00.211
She'd been promoted every year

00:01:00.211 --> 00:01:01.892
for five years in a row,

00:01:01.892 --> 00:01:03.548
was making a fantastic salary

00:01:03.548 --> 00:01:05.728
and was considered to be a rising star

00:01:05.728 --> 00:01:07.369
at her company.

00:01:07.369 --> 00:01:09.615
But staying up until
three every night dancing

00:01:09.615 --> 00:01:12.112
and waking up early to go to her real job

00:01:12.112 --> 00:01:14.206
was taking it's toll.

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:17.661
Then she was forced to make
an impossible decision.

00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:21.047
Going out to practice every
night made her a better dancer.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.534
Pretty soon, the owner of a
local ballroom dance school

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:24.856
asked her to teach for him.

00:01:24.856 --> 00:01:26.847
And then she spun off
her own salsa classes

00:01:26.847 --> 00:01:28.841
as her own business.

00:01:28.841 --> 00:01:30.531
Suddenly what she was doing for fun

00:01:30.531 --> 00:01:33.156
could be a full time opportunity

00:01:33.156 --> 00:01:37.323
but it would mean giving up
her blossoming HR career.

00:01:38.323 --> 00:01:39.677
She made the decision with her heart

00:01:39.677 --> 00:01:43.050
and knew she would never be as happy

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.484
as when she was dancing.

00:01:44.484 --> 00:01:48.126
She gave up her job to
launch Toronto Dance Salsa.

00:01:48.126 --> 00:01:49.638
Willing to live on a much smaller salary

00:01:49.638 --> 00:01:51.582
if it meant she'd be happy.

00:01:51.582 --> 00:01:53.709
She never anticipated that she'd go

00:01:53.709 --> 00:01:54.560
from teaching a few classes a week

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.843
to building a half million dollar business

00:01:56.843 --> 00:01:59.289
with multiple locations.

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:00.967
She simply set out to create a place

00:02:00.967 --> 00:02:03.147
where everyone is included in the fun

00:02:03.147 --> 00:02:07.653
and where everyone feels
at home, like family.

00:02:07.653 --> 00:02:09.259
And that's why her family has grown

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:12.301
to almost 6,000 students,
learning salsa each year,

00:02:12.301 --> 00:02:14.519
making TDS one of the
largest salsa studios

00:02:14.519 --> 00:02:16.634
in North America.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:19.022
TDS makes everyone feel
a part of the family

00:02:19.022 --> 00:02:20.660
with birthday dances for students

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.476
and outings to salsa clubs.

00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:24.320
They have helpers who
are excited to volunteer

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.212
their time so students
get hands-on feedback.

00:02:27.212 --> 00:02:28.733
Helpers and staff alike are brought on

00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:31.038
based on whether they embody family,

00:02:31.038 --> 00:02:32.944
which is more important
to Sharon than talent.

00:02:32.944 --> 00:02:36.051
Her students feel loved and welcome,

00:02:36.051 --> 00:02:37.829
no matter their skill,

00:02:37.829 --> 00:02:39.656
just like she felt when she started.

00:02:39.656 --> 00:02:42.707
Family is what made Sharon happy

00:02:42.707 --> 00:02:44.261
and what connects everything together

00:02:44.261 --> 00:02:46.344
for her growing business.

